  "rationale": "Block h1_0:access and h3_0:reach. Blocking h1_0:access makes h2_2:traverse unreachable, because h2_2 is an AND step that needs h1_0. That in turn removes h4_0:pivot and h4_2:obtain, since both depend only on h2_2. It also removes h3_1:traverse, which depends only on h1_0. After that, the only remaining route is crown <- h4_1:obtain <- h3_0:reach <- h2_0:traverse, and blocking h3_0 cuts it. No single block is enough. Blocking h1_0 alone leaves the h2_0 -> h3_0 -> h4_1 route. Blocking h2_2 alone leaves h1_0 -> h3_1 -> h4_1. Blocking h4_1 alone leaves h4_0 and h4_2. Every other single block leaves h2_2 reachable, and h2_2 reaches crown through h4_0. So the minimum is 2."
